{
  "$comment": "Pinned upstream SOURCE of the Mossaic VFS SDK. Upstream publishes no npm package, so vendoring the source is the only integration path and this file is the substitute for a version range. Every path below is upstream bytes at `commit`, at the same relative path upstream uses, because the SDK reaches its siblings by relative specifier (`../../shared/*`, `../../worker/core/*`) and by the `@shared/*` alias that sdk/tsconfig.json and sdk/tsdown.config.ts both resolve to `../shared`. Flattening the layout would break the build and the aliases at once. `scripts/mossaic-sdk.ts` verifies these digests and then runs the upstream build; the root `prepare` hook runs it after every install. Refresh by re-extracting the closure at a new commit -- `git archive --format=tar <sha> sdk shared worker/core tsconfig.base.json | tar -x -C third_party/mossaic` -- and rewriting `commit`/`vendored` from the new bytes.",
